      "title": "Ram Temple donations theft: SC says ball is in SIT’s court, suggestions can be directed to Solicitor General’s office",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/ram-temple-donations-theft-sc-says-ball-is-in-sits-court-suggestions-can-be-directed-to-solicitor-generals-office/article71355657.ece",
      "description": "Conveying a hands-off approach into the probe on the case, the Bench headed by CJI Surya Kant says if the Special Investigation Team is ‘doing its job satisfactorily, well and good, but if more is required, we will intervene’",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-08-17T10:51:11"
    },
    {
      "title": "Ram Temple donations row: SC asks SIT to conclude probe, file status report",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/ram-temple-donations-row-sc-asks-sit-to-conclude-probe-file-status-report-126081700646_1.html",
      "description": "The Supreme Court on Monday asked a court-appointed Special Investigation Team (SIT) probing the alleged embezzlement of donations at the Ram temple in Ayodhya to complete its investigation expeditiously and take it to a logical conclusion.\nA bench of Chief Justice Surya Kant and Justices Joymalya Bagchi and V Mohana directed the SIT to file its status report in a sealed cover on the progress made in the investigation into the donations theft case.\nThe bench also asked the SIT to consider objectively any suggestions made by the different litigants before the court for qualitative improvement of the investigation and its transparency.\nThe bench said after examining the report of the SIT, the court may issue certain directions for reforms in the management of donations made by the devotees visiting the Ram temple.\nOn July 27, the top court took note of the setting up of the four-member SIT headed by IGP Kiran S to probe the alleged embezzlement of donations at the Ram temple.\nIt had",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-17T09:15:34"
    }
